# IBM watsonx.ai credentials for the Granite narration layer.
#
# These are OPTIONAL. Without them the app runs exactly the same, computes
# exactly the same sky, and narrates it with the built-in deterministic
# narrator instead; the interface says which one is speaking.
#
# Copy to `.env` for local development, or set them as environment variables
# on your host. They are read server-side only and never reach the browser.
#
# Once filled in, check them with:  npm run verify:granite

# Required to enable Granite.
# IBM Cloud console > Manage > Access (IAM) > API keys > Create.
# The value is shown once. There is no way to read it back later.
WATSONX_API_KEY=

# Required to enable Granite.
# watsonx.ai > your project > Manage tab > General > Project ID.
WATSONX_PROJECT_ID=

# Optional. The regional endpoint your watsonx instance lives in. It must match
# the region the project was created in, or every request 404s on the project.
#   https://us-south.ml.cloud.ibm.com   (Dallas, the default)
#   https://eu-gb.ml.cloud.ibm.com      (London)
#   https://eu-de.ml.cloud.ibm.com      (Frankfurt)
#   https://jp-tok.ml.cloud.ibm.com     (Tokyo)
#   https://au-syd.ml.cloud.ibm.com     (Sydney)
WATSONX_URL=

# Optional. Pins one Granite model instead of letting the endpoint pick.
# Leave blank and it tries, in order:
#   ibm/granite-3-3-8b-instruct
#   ibm/granite-4-h-small
#   ibm/granite-3-2-8b-instruct
#   ibm/granite-3-8b-instruct
# Which of these a project can actually call depends on its region and plan.
# `npm run verify:granite` prints the ones yours is offered.
WATSONX_MODEL_ID=

# --- local Granite, for development only -------------------------------------
#
# IBM publishes the Granite weights under Apache 2.0, so the model behind a
# watsonx deployment is one you can run yourself. Set this and the endpoint will
# fall back to it when watsonx cannot answer, naming it in the interface so
# nobody mistakes a local answer for a hosted one.
#
# It exists so the tool-calling loop can be built and exercised without spending
# a hosted token on every malformed argument. watsonx is always tried first, and
# it is the only path that counts as the real one.
#
#   ollama pull granite3.3:8b
#
# Leave unset in any deployment that matters.
# OLLAMA_MODEL=granite3.3:8b
# OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434

# Origins this deployment will answer /api/ask and /api/embed for.
#
# Comma separated, no trailing slash needed. Leave it unset and the endpoints
# answer anybody, which is what you want locally, behind a dev tunnel, and in a
# fresh clone. Set it once the app has a permanent address:
#
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://borrowed-sky.vercel.app
#
# What this buys: another website cannot put this app's AI behind its own page,
# because browsers set Origin on cross-site requests and will not let script
# forge it. What it does not buy: anything against a caller that is not a
# browser, which can omit the header entirely. It raises the cost of casual
# misuse and does nothing about a determined one. See api/_lib/guard.ts.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
